---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<ol class="flow">
  <li>
    <span class="tile">
      <Icon name="download" />
    </span>
    <b>1</b>
    <strong>You open a tool</strong>
    <p>Your browser downloads the tool's code once, like any web page.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="tile">
      <Icon name="zap" />
    </span>
    <b>2</b>
    <strong>Your browser does the work</strong>
    <p>
      Your file is read and edited in your device's memory. It isn't sent
      anywhere.
    </p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <span class="tile">
      <Icon name="check" />
    </span>
    <b>3</b>
    <strong>You save the result</strong>
    <p>
      The finished file goes straight to your downloads. Your original stays
      untouched.
    </p>
  </li>
</ol>

<div class="duo">
  <section class="card-block">
    <span class="tile">
      <Icon name="shield" />
    </span>
    <h2>Blocked by design</h2>
    <p>
      Every kmra site sends a security policy that stops the page from
      contacting any other server. Even if there were a bug, your browser would
      refuse to send your file anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="card-block">
    <span class="tile">
      <Icon name="search" />
    </span>
    <h2>Check it yourself</h2>
    <ol class="mini-steps">
      <li>Open your browser's developer tools.</li>
      <li>Choose the Network tab.</li>
      <li>Use any tool. Nothing is sent while your file is processed.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</div>
